{"id":"679063443","kind":"article","title":"阅读理解","author":"Andy Matuschak","original_authors":["Andy Matuschak"],"original_source_urls":["https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zMybAxZcdkJHKSATuSZbEhz"],"publisher":"Jarrett Ye","column":"认知基石 & 教育培训","date":"2024-01-22","updated":"2024-01-25","votes":39,"comment_count":0,"minutes":1,"chars":583,"keywords":["阅读理解","自我解释","附加问题","助记媒介","元认知"],"summary":"Andy Matuschak 的笔记汇总其阅读理解研究兴趣：读者常在一开始就未真正加工文本，却对自己把握主旨过度自信。作者列举自我解释、附加问题、记忆卡片和助记媒介等潜在干预，认为嵌入练习或可促使读者慢下来并发现理解漏洞。","zhihu_url":"https://zhuanlan.zhihu.com/p/679063443","restoration":null,"toc":[{"id":"sec-1","level":2,"title":"链接至本文（已汉化）"},{"id":"sec-2","level":2,"title":"声明"}],"html":"<p data-pid=\"tJlZ_i3s\">我最感兴趣的是成年人的阅读理解，尤其是难懂的解释文本。一些笔记：</p><ul><li data-pid=\"qp4grc2v\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z59PYkSdPeznr95fco4GRQx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">人们经常难以回忆起文本的细节，原因在于他们起初就根本没有加工文本</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-1\"><a href=\"#ref-1\">[1]</a></sup><br/> </li><ul><li data-pid=\"D2k0YU3_\"> （见 2023-06-30, 2023-08-01, 2023-08-31 patron letters）<br/> </li></ul><li data-pid=\"FUibGy02\"> 干预措施<br/> </li><ul><li data-pid=\"-O3_xas6\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zSoTbuyrXFnDHibaSeEzPRx\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">附加问题</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-2\"><a href=\"#ref-2\">[2]</a></sup><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"YdtKuBEK\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zLZUS7KTrG4ABm3tRLGxMMj\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">阅读理解问题可以发现文本基础的漏洞</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-3\"><a href=\"#ref-3\">[3]</a></sup><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"H4pUZfy_\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zVKwVczp4nEAKPWqfS1BqMi\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">阅读理解问题令人不快</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-4\"><a href=\"#ref-4\">[4]</a></sup><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"Fx_4RLmP\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zAkgXnwHwuvrTjaFM49S5P1\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">教材的习题集并不善于检测阅读理解问题</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-5\"><a href=\"#ref-5\">[5]</a></sup><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"Pto8qW-M\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z4m9Gat7zi9YUmZzQRR7pwt\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">附加问题能够提高学习者对相关但未直接测试的内容的理解</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-6\"><a href=\"#ref-6\">[6]</a></sup><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"agMUS7Wp\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z5aepnaCuu6XiPqB4LgBDkH\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">助记媒介可能会促使读者更缓慢、更专注地阅读</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-7\"><a href=\"#ref-7\">[7]</a></sup><br/> </li></ul><li data-pid=\"9mmTjLUP\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zCQYRYZTQRmrR4bFGCzCMkR\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">自我解释</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-8\"><a href=\"#ref-8\">[8]</a></sup><br/> </li><ul><li data-pid=\"j1hTlXHI\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zUR6RM21Sa88cFDfC47svVv\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">精细口头复述</a><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"bcHK8r1I\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zVXYW2pJPC8iY8JhCCRKbMp\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">iSTART</a><br/> </li><li data-pid=\"zeFw3cXC\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/z7FLRWQNjaUQSvRQJYiqNQm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">McNamara, D. (2004). SERT: Self-explanation reading training. Discourse Processes, 38(1), 1–30</a><br/> </li></ul><li data-pid=\"Uq1LEsWk\"><a class=\"wrap external\" href=\"https://notes.andymatuschak.org/zSv7fL6SRMchq1bvuoQjrxz\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">编写卡片有助于阅读理解</a><sup class=\"cite\" id=\"cite-9\"><a href=\"#ref-9\">[9]</a></sup><br/> </li></ul><h2 id=\"sec-1\">链接至本文（已汉化）</h2><ul><li data-pid=\"T6estu3q\"><a class=\"internal tm-internal\"